commit f12c00b9115f9de0a20df947c97a8dbdf71e1eb8
Author: tvofi <70032254+tvofi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 22:25:59 2026 +0000

    F1.8: a held unique id is left alone; currency is derived, not multi-written
    
    #1799 review B1: identity_update wrote a re-derived unique id without
    asking whether another heatpump_optimizer entry already held it, so
    editing a stale D10-s1-01 duplicate would index two entries under one id
    (real Home Assistant 2026.9.3 logs that as an integration error). It now
    takes hass and returns {} when async_entry_for_domain_unique_id finds
    another entry, as the reconfigure step aborts there. Reauth, both
    options-save exits and assign_entity pass hass. Pinned in
    tests/entities.py; the check fails with the guard removed.
    
    Ratchet: coordinator.currency is now a class property, the feed code
    adopted per cycle (_feed_code, one writer in _update_current_state) or,
    before the first cycle, the feed's live declaration, else the configured
    currency. The __init__ write is gone, so coordinator_multiassigned_attrs
    stays at 116 and the budget is restored to 116; coordinator_loc and
    coordinator_attrs are unchanged.
    
    Optional review note: declared_currency reads an ISO code only as three
    ASCII letters, so "ÖRE/kWh" declares nothing (pinned in features.py).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pj9jmSDxWihZsBLYgyTqbE

